\pard\f3\b\fs28\fi-1020\li1200\fc0\cf0 Class Description\

\fs14 \

\pard\tx3600\tx3980\tx4340\f0\b0\fs28\li1500\fc0\cf0 NSTimeZone is an abstract class that refines the behavior provided by NSTimeZone. NSTimeZone identifies a geopolitical region with a name (such as ªUS/Pacificº). NSTimeZoneDetail augments this region name with more specific information appropriate for a particular date within its geopolitical region: an abbreviation, an offset (in seconds) from Greenwich Mean Time (GMT), and an indication of whether this is a Daylight Savings Time time zone. The specificity afforded through NSTimeZoneDetail helps to resolve conflicts between abbreviations and offsets that can arise within regions.\

\fs14 \

\fs28 Even though it is an abstract subclass of NSTimeZone, NSTimeZoneDetail does 
\i not
\i0  have class methods that create and return time zone objects. See the specification of NSTimeZone for creation methods.\

\fs14 \

\fs28 However, NSTimeZoneDetail does have accessor methods that allow you to get the abbreviation and temporal offset of a time zone object, as well as determine whether this is a Daylight Savings Time time zone.\

\fs14 \

